* text=auto eol=lf

# Vendored third-party attribution text, kept byte-identical to what upstream
# ships — a licensing artifact, not source to reformat.
#
# Git already leaves it alone, but for an incidental reason: the file contains a
# lone CR among its 21 CRLF endings, which makes `text=auto` classify it as
# binary and skip conversion. Verified — under `text=auto` a pure-CRLF file is
# normalized on add while an otherwise identical file with one lone CR is not.
#
# That is a side effect of one stray byte, not a decision. `-text` states the
# intent outright, so the file is preserved because it is meant to be rather
# than because a heuristic happens to spare it, and a reader who finds CRLF in a
# repo that mandates LF has the reason next to the rule.
public/office-sprites/kenney/ATTRIBUTION-KENNEY.txt -text
